    "long_instructions": "## Video Game Reviews\r\n\r\nUse `video_game_reviews.csv` to practice filtering and aggregating data.\r\n\r\n::: details [✅ Step 1]\r\nCreate a filtered DataFrame containing reviews that:\r\n\r\n- Have a `Rating` greater than or equal to `9.5`\r\n- Have a non-null `Platform`\r\n\r\nUse AND (`&`) to combine the conditions. Print the first five rows.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [✅ Step 2]\r\nCreate a filtered DataFrame containing reviews whose `Game Title` ends with `\"2\"`. Print the first five rows.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [✅ Step 3]\r\nCreate a filtered DataFrame containing reviews that:\r\n\r\n- Have a `Rating` greater than or equal to `8`\r\n- Have a `Comment Count` greater than `100`\r\n- Have a `Platform` of either `\"PS5\"` or `\"XBSX\"`\r\n\r\nUse parentheses to group the two Platform conditions. Print the first five rows.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [✅ Step 4]\r\nGroup the data by `Year`. Calculate the count and median of `Rating` for each year. Print the summary.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [Need Help?]\r\nUse AI Tutor to look up pandas documentation, explain your filter, or request a hint. When debugging a compound filter, check what each condition returns before combining the conditions.\r\n:::",
